                <pb facs="0355" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v06/pg321"/>

                <head>62. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On April 1, the White House released identical letters from President
                        Eisenhower to Vice President Nixon and Speaker of the House of
                    Representatives Sam Rayburn supporting acceleration of the Inter-American
                    Highway construction program. The letters indicate that the President would soon
                    transmit to Congress a request to authorize appropriation of approximately $75
                    million for such purpose. For text, see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, April 11, 1955, pages 595–596.
                    Appropriation legislation was subsequently enacted as Public Law 129, approved
                    July 1, 1955 (69 Stat. 244), and Public Law 219, approved August 4, 1955 (69
                    Stat. 452).</p>
            </div>
